IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 3 (continued): ss 23 to 29: space and facilities in land and buildings, radio-communication facilities, directions to provide space,
-- exclusive agreements, compensation disputes, precautions, exemption from distress.
-- Seat: the developer, owner or occupier of the land or building, and the telecommunication licensee the code or direction reaches.
-- Where this module says a person "must comply", the fact asked for is the one that triggers the duty.

§ `s 23 Provision of space or facility under code of practice`

-- src:1758 | 23.—(1) The Authority may, from time to time —
-- src:1760 | (a) issue one or more codes of practice for or in connection
-- src:1761 | with the provision, maintenance and use of, and access to,
-- src:1762 | space and facilities within or on any land or building for the
-- src:1763 | operation of any installation, plant or system used for
-- src:1764 | telecommunications, and the allocation of costs and
-- src:1765 | expenses incurred for such provision, maintenance, use
-- src:1766 | and access; and
-- src:1768 | (b) amend, suspend or revoke the whole or any part of any
-- src:1769 | code of practice issued under paragraph (a).
@ref s 23(1) (src:1758-1769)
GIVEN `the code of practice is for or in connection with the provision, maintenance and use of, and access to, space and facilities within or on land or a building for the operation of installation, plant or a system used for telecommunications, and the allocation of costs and expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(1): the Authority may issue, and amend, suspend or revoke, the code of practice` MEANS
    `the code of practice is for or in connection with the provision, maintenance and use of, and access to, space and facilities within or on land or a building for the operation of installation, plant or a system used for telecommunications, and the allocation of costs and expenses`

-- src:1773 | (2) A code of practice issued under subsection (1) may, in
-- src:1774 | particular —
-- src:1776 | (a) require the developer or owner of any land or building to
-- src:1777 | provide, maintain or give access to, at the developer’s or
-- src:1778 | owner’s expense, such space or facility within or on the
-- src:1779 | land or building, for the installation, operation or
-- src:1780 | maintenance of any installation, plant or system used for
-- src:1781 | either or both of the following purposes:
-- src:1783 | (i) the provision of any telecommunication service or
-- src:1784 | radio‑communication service to that land or
-- src:1785 | building;
-- src:1787 | (ii) the provision of any telecommunication service or
-- src:1788 | radio‑communication service to any other land or
-- src:1789 | building; and
-- src:1791 | (b) provide for such fees and charges as may be payable to the
-- src:1792 | Authority in relation to any application or request made to
-- src:1793 | the Authority under the code of practice.
@ref s 23(2) (src:1773-1793)
GIVEN `the person is the developer or owner of the land or building` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the space or facility is for the installation, operation or maintenance of installation, plant or a system used for providing a telecommunication service or radio-communication service to that land or building, or to another land or building` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(2)(a): the code of practice may require the person to provide, maintain or give access to the space or facility at the person's own expense` MEANS
    `the person is the developer or owner of the land or building` AND `the space or facility is for the installation, operation or maintenance of installation, plant or a system used for providing a telecommunication service or radio-communication service to that land or building, or to another land or building`

GIVEN `the fee or charge is payable to the Authority in relation to an application or request made to the Authority under the code of practice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(2)(b): the code of practice may provide for the fee or charge` MEANS
    `the fee or charge is payable to the Authority in relation to an application or request made to the Authority under the code of practice`

-- src:1797 | (3) If any provision in any code of practice issued under
-- src:1798 | subsection (1) is inconsistent with any provision of this Act, that
-- src:1799 | provision in that code of practice, to the extent of the inconsistency —
-- src:1801 | (a) has effect subject to the provisions of this Act; or
-- src:1803 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1804 | 37 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:1806 | (b) having regard to the provisions of this Act, does not have
-- src:1807 | effect.
-- src:1809 | [19/2011]
-- src:1811 | (4) A code of practice issued under subsection (1) does not have
-- src:1812 | legislative effect.
-- src:1814 | [19/2011]
@ref s 23(3) and (4) (src:1797-1814)
GIVEN `a provision of the code of practice is inconsistent with a provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(3): the code provision has effect only subject to the Act, or has no effect, to the extent of the inconsistency` MEANS
    `a provision of the code of practice is inconsistent with a provision of this Act`

GIVEN `the code of practice was issued under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(4): the code of practice has legislative effect` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:1816 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), every developer or owner of any land
-- src:1817 | or building, and every telecommunication licensee, to whom any
-- src:1818 | code of practice issued under subsection (1) applies must comply, at
-- src:1819 | that person’s expense, with that code of practice.
-- src:1821 | [19/2011]
-- src:1823 | (6) The Authority may, either generally or for such time as the
-- src:1824 | Authority may specify, waive the application, to any developer or
-- src:1825 | owner of any land or building or to any telecommunication licensee,
-- src:1826 | of any code of practice issued under subsection (1) or of any part
-- src:1827 | thereof.
@ref s 23(5) and (6) (src:1816-1827)
GIVEN `the code of practice issued under subsection (1) applies to the developer, owner or telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority waived the application of the code or part of it, generally or for such time as it specified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(5): the developer, owner or telecommunication licensee must comply, at that person's expense, with the code of practice` MEANS
    `the code of practice issued under subsection (1) applies to the developer, owner or telecommunication licensee` AND (NOT `the Authority waived the application of the code or part of it, generally or for such time as it specified`)

-- src:1831 | (7) The Authority may give a written notice to a telecommunication
-- src:1832 | licensee, or a developer, owner or occupier of any land or building,
-- src:1833 | requiring compliance with any code of practice issued under
-- src:1834 | subsection (1).
-- src:1836 | [30/2016]
-- src:1838 | (8) The Authority may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the
-- src:1839 | whole or any part of a written notice given under subsection (7).
-- src:1841 | [30/2016]
-- src:1843 | (9) To avoid doubt, the Authority may give a written notice under
-- src:1844 | subsection (7) even though such written notice may prejudice the
-- src:1845 | contractual obligations of the telecommunication licensee, or the
-- src:1846 | developer, owner or occupier of any land or building, whether the
-- src:1847 | obligation relates to a contract made before, on or after 1 February
-- src:1848 | 2017.
-- src:1850 | [30/2016]
-- src:1852 | (10) No liability shall lie against any party to a contract made
-- src:1853 | before, on or after 1 February 2017 for or in relation to, any breach of
-- src:1854 | the contract where the breach is solely attributable to, or occasioned
-- src:1855 | by, the compliance by that party with any written notice given under
-- src:1856 | subsection (7).
@ref s 23(7) to (10) (src:1831-1856)
GIVEN `the person is a telecommunication licensee, or a developer, owner or occupier of land or a building` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(7): the Authority may give the person a written notice requiring compliance with the code of practice` MEANS
    `the person is a telecommunication licensee, or a developer, owner or occupier of land or a building`

GIVEN `the written notice given under subsection (7) may prejudice the contractual obligations of the telecommunication licensee, or the developer, owner or occupier, whether the contract was made before, on or after 1 February 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(9): the prejudice to contractual obligations bars the Authority from giving the written notice` MEANS
    FALSE

GIVEN `the Authority varies, suspends or revokes the whole or any part of a written notice given under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(8): the Authority may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the written notice` MEANS
    `the Authority varies, suspends or revokes the whole or any part of a written notice given under subsection (7)`

GIVEN `the breach of the contract is solely attributable to, or occasioned by, the party's compliance with a written notice given under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(10): the party is liable for the breach of the contract` MEANS
    NOT `the breach of the contract is solely attributable to, or occasioned by, the party's compliance with a written notice given under subsection (7)`

-- src:1863 | (11) Subsection (10) does not affect the operation of the Frustrated
-- src:1864 | Contracts Act 1959.
@ref s 23(11) (src:1863-1864)
GIVEN `the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959 would otherwise operate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(11): subsection (10) affects the operation of the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:1868 | (12) Where any code of practice issued under subsection (1) applies
-- src:1869 | to a person who is a developer or an owner of any land or building,
-- src:1870 | and the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has
-- src:1871 | contravened, whether by act or omission, any provision of that code
-- src:1872 | of practice, the Authority may issue such written order to the person
-- src:1873 | as the Authority considers necessary for the purpose of securing
-- src:1874 | compliance with that provision.
@ref s 23(12) (src:1868-1874)
GIVEN `the code of practice applies to the person, a developer or owner of land or a building` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has contravened, by act or omission, a provision of the code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(12): the Authority may issue the written order the Authority considers necessary to secure compliance` MEANS
    `the code of practice applies to the person, a developer or owner of land or a building` AND `the Authority is satisfied that the person is contravening, or has contravened, by act or omission, a provision of the code`

-- src:1878 | (13) An order under subsection (12) —
-- src:1880 | (a) may require the person concerned (according to the
-- src:1881 | circumstances of the case) to do, or to refrain from
-- src:1882 | doing, such things as are specified in the order, or as are of
-- src:1883 | a description specified in the order; and
-- src:1885 | (b) takes effect at such time (being the earliest practicable
-- src:1886 | time) as is determined by or under that order.
-- src:1888 | [19/2011]
-- src:1890 | (14) The Authority may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the
-- src:1891 | whole or any part of an order under subsection (12).
-- src:1893 | [19/2011]
@ref s 23(13) and (14) (src:1878-1893)
GIVEN `the thing is specified in the order or is of a description specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(13)(a): the order may require the person to do, or refrain from doing, the thing` MEANS
    `the thing is specified in the order or is of a description specified in the order`

GIVEN `the time is the earliest practicable time determined by or under the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(13)(b): the order takes effect at this time` MEANS
    `the time is the earliest practicable time determined by or under the order`

GIVEN `the Authority varies, suspends or revokes the whole or any part of an order under subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(14): the Authority may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the order` MEANS
    `the Authority varies, suspends or revokes the whole or any part of an order under subsection (12)`

-- src:1895 | (15) Any person referred to in subsection (12) who fails to comply
-- src:1896 | with an order under that subsection shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 23(15) (src:1895-1896)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with an order under subsection (12)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(15): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person fails to comply with an order under subsection (12)`

-- src:1900 | (16) Any relevant specifications in force immediately before
-- src:1901 | 1 February 2012 —
-- src:1903 | (a) are deemed to be a code of practice issued under
-- src:1904 | subsection (1); and
-- src:1906 | (b) remain in force until revoked or replaced by a code of
-- src:1907 | practice issued under subsection (1).
-- src:1909 | [19/2011]
-- src:1911 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1912 | 39 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:1914 | (17) In subsection (16) “relevant specifications” means any
-- src:1915 | specifications published by the Authority under section 23 in force
-- src:1916 | immediately before 1 February 2012.
@ref s 23(16) and (17) (src:1900-1916)
GIVEN `the specification was published by the Authority under section 23 and in force immediately before 1 February 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been revoked or replaced by a code of practice issued under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(16): the relevant specification is deemed to be a code of practice issued under subsection (1) and remains in force` MEANS
    `the specification was published by the Authority under section 23 and in force immediately before 1 February 2012` AND (NOT `it has been revoked or replaced by a code of practice issued under subsection (1)`)

§ `s 24 Provision of facilities for radio-communication`

-- src:1924 | 24.—(1) Any person who intends to install, erect or construct,
-- src:1925 | within a radius of 200 metres from the site of a telecommunication
-- src:1926 | licensee’s installation or plant used in connection with its
-- src:1927 | radio‑communication service, any building more than 30 metres
-- src:1928 | above ground level must notify the licensee in writing before carrying
-- src:1929 | out any such installation, erection or construction.
@ref s 24(1) (src:1924-1929)
GIVEN `the person intends to install, erect or construct a building more than 30 metres above ground level` IS A BOOLEAN
      `metres from the site of the telecommunication licensee's installation or plant used in connection with its radio-communication service` IS A NUMBER
      `the person notified the licensee in writing before carrying out the installation, erection or construction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(1): the person has done what the subsection requires` MEANS
    (NOT (`the person intends to install, erect or construct a building more than 30 metres above ground level` AND (`metres from the site of the telecommunication licensee's installation or plant used in connection with its radio-communication service` AT MOST 200))) OR `the person notified the licensee in writing before carrying out the installation, erection or construction`

-- src:1931 | (2) The telecommunication licensee may, after receiving such
-- src:1932 | notification from the person, make arrangements with the person for
-- src:1933 | the licensee to enter upon the building at any reasonable time to
-- src:1934 | provide such accommodation or other facilities in or around the
-- src:1935 | building as may be necessary or proper for any installation or plant
-- src:1936 | used in connection with radio‑communication service to be laid,
-- src:1937 | placed, constructed, erected or installed in, on or around the building.
@ref s 24(2) (src:1931-1937)
GIVEN `the licensee received notification from the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(2): the licensee may make arrangements with the person to enter upon the building at a reasonable time and provide the accommodation or facilities` MEANS
    `the licensee received notification from the person`

-- src:1939 | (3) Where, in the opinion of a telecommunication licensee, a
-- src:1940 | building which is installed, erected or constructed after the licensee’s
-- src:1941 | installation or plant used in connection with its radio‑communication
-- src:1942 | service was laid, placed, constructed, erected or installed in or around
-- src:1943 | the building, interrupts or interferes with the licensee’s
-- src:1944 | radio‑communication service or system, the licensee may, with the
-- src:1945 | approval of the Authority, at any reasonable time, enter upon the
-- src:1946 | building to provide such accommodation or other facilities in or
-- src:1947 | around the building as may be necessary or proper for such
-- src:1948 | installation or plant to be laid, placed, constructed, erected or
-- src:1949 | installed in, on or around the building for the purposes of eliminating
-- src:1950 | such interruption or interference.
@ref s 24(3) (src:1939-1950)
GIVEN `the building was installed, erected or constructed after the licensee's installation or plant was laid, placed, constructed, erected or installed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the licensee the building interrupts or interferes with the licensee's radio-communication service or system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(3): the licensee may at any reasonable time enter upon the building to provide the accommodation or facilities necessary to eliminate the interruption or interference` MEANS
    `the building was installed, erected or constructed after the licensee's installation or plant was laid, placed, constructed, erected or installed` AND `in the opinion of the licensee the building interrupts or interferes with the licensee's radio-communication service or system` AND `the Authority approved`

-- src:1952 | (4) The telecommunication licensee must pay compensation to the
-- src:1953 | owner or occupier of any building for any disturbance, disability or
-- src:1954 | damage caused as a result of any act of the licensee under
-- src:1955 | subsection (2) or (3).
@ref s 24(4) (src:1952-1955)
GIVEN `the licensee did an act under subsection (2) or (3) that caused disturbance, disability or damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(4): the licensee must pay compensation to the owner or occupier of the building` MEANS
    `the licensee did an act under subsection (2) or (3) that caused disturbance, disability or damage`

-- src:1960 | (5) In this section and section 23, “building” means any permanent
-- src:1961 | or temporary building and includes any structure or erection of any
-- src:1962 | kind (whether permanent or temporary) and any extension,
-- src:1963 | modification or alteration made thereto.
@ref s 24(5) (src:1960-1963)
GIVEN `it is a permanent or temporary building, or a structure or erection of any kind, permanent or temporary, or an extension, modification or alteration made to one` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 24(5): this is a "building" in section 24 and section 23` MEANS
    `it is a permanent or temporary building, or a structure or erection of any kind, permanent or temporary, or an extension, modification or alteration made to one`

§ `s 25 Provision of space or facility or installation, plant or system by direction of Authority`

-- src:1970 | 25.—(1) Where the Authority considers it necessary that any
-- src:1971 | telecommunication service should be provided to any land or
-- src:1972 | building (whether completed or not) or any occupier of the land or
-- src:1973 | building, or that the quality of a telecommunication service provided
-- src:1974 | to any land or building or to any occupier of that land or building
-- src:1975 | should be enhanced, the Authority may by direction —
-- src:1977 | (a) require the developer or owner of the land or building to
-- src:1978 | provide, at the developer’s or owner’s expense and within
-- src:1979 | such period as may be specified in the direction, such space
-- src:1980 | or facility within or on that land or building, and access to
-- src:1981 | that land or building, as the Authority may specify in its
-- src:1982 | direction; and
-- src:1984 | (b) require any telecommunication licensee to install, within
-- src:1985 | such period as may be specified in the direction, such
-- src:1986 | installation, plant or system in that space or facility as the
-- src:1987 | Authority considers necessary for the provision, or the
-- src:1988 | enhancement of quality, of the telecommunication service
-- src:1989 | to that land or building or to the occupier of that land or
-- src:1990 | building.
@ref s 25(1) (src:1970-1990)
GIVEN `the Authority considers it necessary that a telecommunication service should be provided to land or a building (whether completed or not) or its occupier, or that the quality of the service provided should be enhanced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the developer or owner of the land or building` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(1): the Authority may by direction require the person to provide the space, facility and access at the developer's or owner's expense, or to install the installation, plant or system within the period specified` MEANS
    `the Authority considers it necessary that a telecommunication service should be provided to land or a building (whether completed or not) or its occupier, or that the quality of the service provided should be enhanced` AND (`the person is the developer or owner of the land or building` OR `the person is a telecommunication licensee`)

-- src:1994 | (2) Where the Authority considers it necessary that any
-- src:1995 | broadcasting service, the operation of which requires a
-- src:1996 | telecommunication system, should be provided to any land or
-- src:1997 | building, whether completed or not, or that the quality of any such
-- src:1998 | broadcasting service provided to any land or building should be
-- src:1999 | enhanced, the Authority may by direction —
-- src:2001 | (a) require the developer or owner of the land or building to
-- src:2002 | provide at the developer’s or owner’s expense and within
-- src:2003 | such period as may be specified in the direction, such space
-- src:2005 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:2006 | 41 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:2008 | or facility within or on the land or building, and access
-- src:2009 | thereto, as the Authority may specify in its direction; and
-- src:2011 | (b) require any telecommunication licensee to install, within
-- src:2012 | such period as may be specified in the direction, such
-- src:2013 | installation, plant or system as the Authority considers
-- src:2014 | necessary for the provision, or the enhancement of quality,
-- src:2015 | of the broadcasting service to the land or building.
@ref s 25(2) (src:1994-2015)
GIVEN `the Authority considers it necessary that a broadcasting service, the operation of which requires a telecommunication system, should be provided to land or a building (whether completed or not), or that its quality should be enhanced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the developer or owner of the land or building` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(2): the Authority may by direction require the person to provide the space, facility and access, or to install the installation, plant or system, within the period specified` MEANS
    `the Authority considers it necessary that a broadcasting service, the operation of which requires a telecommunication system, should be provided to land or a building (whether completed or not), or that its quality should be enhanced` AND (`the person is the developer or owner of the land or building` OR `the person is a telecommunication licensee`)

-- src:2019 | (3) Where the Authority —
-- src:2021 | (a) considers it necessary that in relation to any land or
-- src:2022 | building, whether completed or not (called in this section
-- src:2023 | the relevant property), a radio‑communication service
-- src:2024 | should be provided to the relevant property or the quality
-- src:2025 | of a radio‑communication service provided to the relevant
-- src:2026 | property should be enhanced; and
-- src:2028 | (b) is satisfied that it would be in the public interest for a
-- src:2029 | telecommunication licensee providing the
-- src:2030 | radio‑communication service to install any installation,
-- src:2031 | plant or system within or on another land or building
-- src:2032 | (called in this section the subject property) in order to serve
-- src:2033 | the relevant property or enhance the quality of the
-- src:2034 | radio‑communication service provided to the relevant
-- src:2035 | property,
-- src:2037 | the Authority may by direction —
-- src:2039 | (c) require the developer or owner of the subject property in
-- src:2040 | paragraph (b) to provide, at the developer’s or owner’s
-- src:2041 | expense and within such period as may be specified in the
-- src:2042 | direction, such space or facility within or on the subject
-- src:2043 | property, and access to the subject property, as the
-- src:2044 | Authority may specify in its direction; and
-- src:2046 | (d) require the telecommunication licensee to install within or
-- src:2047 | on the subject property, within such period as may be
-- src:2048 | specified in the direction, such installation, plant or system
-- src:2049 | as the Authority considers necessary for the provision or
-- src:2051 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:2052 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 42
-- src:2054 | enhancement of the quality of the radio‑communication
-- src:2055 | service to the relevant property.
@ref s 25(3) (src:2019-2055)
GIVEN `the Authority considers it necessary that a radio-communication service should be provided to the relevant property, or its quality enhanced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that it would be in the public interest for the licensee to install installation, plant or system within or on the subject property to serve the relevant property or enhance the quality of service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the developer or owner of the subject property, or the telecommunication licensee providing the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(3): the Authority may by direction require the person to provide the space, facility and access on the subject property, or to install the installation, plant or system there, within the period specified` MEANS
    `the Authority considers it necessary that a radio-communication service should be provided to the relevant property, or its quality enhanced` AND `the Authority is satisfied that it would be in the public interest for the licensee to install installation, plant or system within or on the subject property to serve the relevant property or enhance the quality of service` AND `the person is the developer or owner of the subject property, or the telecommunication licensee providing the service`

-- src:2059 | (4) To avoid doubt, the Authority may give directions under
