GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(5): the party is liable for the breach of the contract` MEANS
    NOT `the breach of the contract is solely attributable to, or occasioned by, the party's compliance with a direction of the Authority under subsection (1), (2), (3) or (13)`

-- src:2076 | (6) Subsection (5) does not affect the operation of the Frustrated
-- src:2077 | Contracts Act 1959.
@ref s 25(6) (src:2076-2077)
GIVEN `the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959 would otherwise operate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(6): subsection (5) affects the operation of the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:2081 | (7) Where a telecommunication licensee that is using any space or
-- src:2082 | facility within or on any land or building pursuant to a direction under
-- src:2083 | subsection (1), (2) or (3), or any code of practice issued by the
-- src:2084 | Authority, intends to use that space or facility —
-- src:2086 | (a) to provide any telecommunication service or broadcasting
-- src:2087 | service, or to enhance the quality of any
-- src:2088 | telecommunication service or broadcasting service
-- src:2089 | provided, to any land or building not in the direction to
-- src:2090 | the licensee under subsection (1) or (2);
-- src:2092 | (b) to provide any radio‑communication service, or to enhance
-- src:2093 | the quality of any radio‑communication service provided,
-- src:2094 | to any land or building that is not the relevant land or
-- src:2095 | building in the direction to the licensee under
-- src:2096 | subsection (3); or
-- src:2098 | (c) to provide any telecommunication service, broadcasting
-- src:2099 | service or radio‑communication service that is not in the
-- src:2100 | direction to the licensee under subsection (1), (2) or (3) (as
-- src:2102 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:2103 | 43 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:2105 | the case may be) whether or not to the same land or
-- src:2106 | building in the direction,
-- src:2108 | the licensee must give 14 days’ notice to the developer or owner of
-- src:2109 | that land or building, stating as fully and accurately as possible the
-- src:2110 | nature and extent of the acts intended to be done for the purpose of
-- src:2111 | paragraph (a), (b) or (c), as the case may be.
@ref s 25(7) (src:2081-2111)
GIVEN `the licensee is using space or facility pursuant to a direction under subsection (1), (2) or (3), or a code of practice issued by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee intends to use it to provide, or enhance the quality of, a telecommunication service, broadcasting service or radio-communication service not in the direction, or to land or a building not in the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days of notice given to the developer or owner, stating as fully and accurately as possible the nature and extent of the acts intended to be done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(7): the licensee has given the notice the subsection requires` MEANS
    (NOT (`the licensee is using space or facility pursuant to a direction under subsection (1), (2) or (3), or a code of practice issued by the Authority` AND `the licensee intends to use it to provide, or enhance the quality of, a telecommunication service, broadcasting service or radio-communication service not in the direction, or to land or a building not in the direction`)) OR (`days of notice given to the developer or owner, stating as fully and accurately as possible the nature and extent of the acts intended to be done` AT LEAST 14)

-- src:2115 | (8) The developer or owner of the land or building may, within
-- src:2116 | 14 days after receiving a notice under subsection (7), lodge a written
-- src:2117 | objection with the Authority.
@ref s 25(8) (src:2115-2117)
GIVEN `days after receiving the notice under subsection (7)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(8): the developer or owner may lodge a written objection with the Authority` MEANS
    `days after receiving the notice under subsection (7)` AT MOST 14

-- src:2121 | (9) Where a written objection is lodged by the developer or owner
-- src:2122 | of the land or building under subsection (8) (called in this section the
-- src:2123 | objector), the Authority must notify the telecommunication licensee
-- src:2124 | concerned to resolve the dispute with the objector due to the
-- src:2125 | objection.
-- src:2127 | [30/2016]
-- src:2129 | (10) On receipt of the Authority’s notice under subsection (9), the
-- src:2130 | telecommunication licensee must take genuine steps to resolve the
-- src:2131 | dispute with the objector due to the objection.
-- src:2133 | [30/2016]
@ref s 25(9) and (10) (src:2121-2133)
GIVEN `a written objection is lodged by the developer or owner under subsection (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(9) and (10): the Authority must notify the licensee to resolve the dispute and the licensee must take genuine steps to resolve it` MEANS
    `a written objection is lodged by the developer or owner under subsection (8)`

-- src:2135 | (11) If the telecommunication licensee fails to resolve the dispute
-- src:2136 | due to the objection, the licensee must inform the Authority in writing
-- src:2137 | and also furnish all relevant information relating to the steps taken by
-- src:2138 | the licensee to resolve the dispute due to the objection.
@ref s 25(11) (src:2135-2138)
GIVEN `the licensee fails to resolve the dispute due to the objection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(11): the licensee must inform the Authority in writing and furnish all relevant information relating to the steps taken` MEANS
    `the licensee fails to resolve the dispute due to the objection`

-- src:2142 | (12) After receipt of the information mentioned in subsection (11),
-- src:2143 | the Authority —
-- src:2145 | (a) must notify the telecommunication licensee and the
-- src:2146 | objector as to whether the Authority is satisfied that the
-- src:2147 | licensee has taken genuine steps to resolve the dispute due
-- src:2148 | to the objection; and
-- src:2150 | (b) if so satisfied, must hold an inquiry (in such manner as the
-- src:2151 | Authority thinks fit) on the objection, giving each party a
-- src:2152 | reasonable opportunity to be heard if the objection is not
-- src:2153 | withdrawn.
@ref s 25(12) (src:2142-2153)
GIVEN `the Authority received the information mentioned in subsection (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the licensee took genuine steps to resolve the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection is not withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(12): the Authority must hold an inquiry on the objection, giving each party a reasonable opportunity to be heard` MEANS
    `the Authority received the information mentioned in subsection (11)` AND `the Authority is satisfied that the licensee took genuine steps to resolve the dispute` AND `the objection is not withdrawn`

-- src:2160 | (13) Upon the conclusion of the inquiry, the Authority may, upon
-- src:2161 | being satisfied that the use of the space or facility for a purpose in the
-- src:2162 | notice given under subsection (7) would be reasonable, by directions
-- src:2163 | to the telecommunication licensee or the developer or owner of the
-- src:2164 | land or building require either or both to give effect to the notice in
-- src:2165 | such manner and on such terms, conditions and stipulations as the
-- src:2166 | Authority may specify in the direction, including directions that —
-- src:2168 | (a) require the developer or owner to allow the licensee to use
-- src:2169 | the space or facility; or
-- src:2171 | (b) require the licensee to install and operate any installation,
-- src:2172 | plant or system within the space or facility.
@ref s 25(13) (src:2160-2172)
GIVEN `the inquiry has concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority is satisfied that the use of the space or facility for a purpose in the notice under subsection (7) would be reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(13): the Authority may by directions require the licensee or the developer or owner, or both, to give effect to the notice in such manner and on such terms as it specifies` MEANS
    `the inquiry has concluded` AND `the Authority is satisfied that the use of the space or facility for a purpose in the notice under subsection (7) would be reasonable`

-- src:2176 | (14) The telecommunication licensee may enter on the land or
-- src:2177 | building and do all or any of the acts mentioned in the notice given
-- src:2178 | under subsection (7) —
-- src:2180 | (a) where no written objection is lodged within the period
-- src:2181 | specified in subsection (8), after the expiry of that period;
-- src:2182 | or
-- src:2184 | (b) where a written objection is lodged under subsection (8) —
-- src:2186 | (i) after the objection is withdrawn;
-- src:2188 | (ii) after the telecommunication licensee resolves the
-- src:2189 | dispute with the objector due to the objection; or
-- src:2191 | (iii) on the Authority’s direction under subsection (13),
-- src:2192 | subject to the terms, conditions and stipulations
-- src:2193 | imposed by the Authority under that subsection.
@ref s 25(14) (src:2176-2193)
GIVEN `no written objection was lodged within the period specified in subsection (8), and the period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written objection was lodged and has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written objection was lodged and the licensee has resolved the dispute with the objector` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written objection was lodged and the Authority has directed under subsection (13), and the licensee acts subject to the terms, conditions and stipulations imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(14): the licensee may enter on the land or building and do the acts mentioned in the notice` MEANS
    `no written objection was lodged within the period specified in subsection (8), and the period has expired` OR `a written objection was lodged and has been withdrawn` OR `a written objection was lodged and the licensee has resolved the dispute with the objector` OR `a written objection was lodged and the Authority has directed under subsection (13), and the licensee acts subject to the terms, conditions and stipulations imposed`

-- src:2197 | (15) Any direction under subsection (1), (2), (3) or (13) may
-- src:2198 | include —
-- src:2200 | (a) a requirement that the telecommunication licensee must
-- src:2201 | contribute, wholly or partly, to such costs and expenses
-- src:2202 | incurred for the provision and use of any space or facility
-- src:2203 | or installation, plant or system under subsection (1), (2),
-- src:2204 | (3) or (13) as the Authority may determine;
-- src:2206 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:2207 | 45 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:2209 | (b) terms and conditions relating to the payment of costs and
-- src:2210 | expenses necessary for any alteration, removal, relocation
-- src:2211 | or diversion of the installation, plant or system that may
-- src:2212 | subsequently be required; and
-- src:2214 | (c) such other requirements as the Authority may specify.
@ref s 25(15) (src:2197-2214)
GIVEN requirement IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(15): a direction under subsection (1), (2), (3) or (13) may include this requirement` MEANS
    elem requirement (LIST "that the telecommunication licensee contribute, wholly or partly, to such costs and expenses incurred for the provision and use of any space, facility, installation, plant or system as the Authority may determine"
                         , "terms and conditions relating to the payment of costs and expenses necessary for any alteration, removal, relocation or diversion of the installation, plant or system that may subsequently be required"
                         , "such other requirements as the Authority may specify")

-- src:2218 | (16) The Authority may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the
-- src:2219 | whole or any part of a direction under subsection (1), (2), (3) or (13).
@ref s 25(16) (src:2218-2219)
GIVEN `the Authority varies, suspends or revokes the whole or any part of a direction under subsection (1), (2), (3) or (13)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(16): the Authority may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the direction` MEANS
    `the Authority varies, suspends or revokes the whole or any part of a direction under subsection (1), (2), (3) or (13)`

-- src:2223 | (17) Any person who fails to comply with any requirement in a
-- src:2224 | direction under this section shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 25(17) (src:2223-2224)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with a requirement in a direction under section 25` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(17): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person fails to comply with a requirement in a direction under section 25`

§ `ss 26 to 29`

-- src:2232 | 26.—(1) The developer or owner of any land or building —
-- src:2234 | (a) must not enter into or enforce any agreement or
-- src:2235 | arrangement with any occupier of the land or building
-- src:2236 | that restricts or prevents the occupier from selecting any
-- src:2237 | supplier of telecommunication systems and services to
-- src:2238 | provide telecommunication services to the occupier; and
-- src:2240 | (b) must not enter into or enforce any agreement or
-- src:2241 | arrangement with any telecommunication licensee that
-- src:2242 | restricts or prevents other telecommunication licensees
-- src:2243 | from installing their installation, plant or system in the land
-- src:2244 | or building or supplying telecommunication systems and
-- src:2245 | services to the land or building or supplying
-- src:2246 | telecommunication services to any occupier of the land
-- src:2247 | or building.
@ref s 26(1) (src:2232-2247)
GIVEN `the developer or owner enters into or enforces an agreement or arrangement with an occupier that restricts or prevents the occupier from selecting any supplier of telecommunication systems and services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the developer or owner enters into or enforces an agreement or arrangement with a telecommunication licensee that restricts or prevents other licensees from installing their installation, plant or system in the land or building, or supplying telecommunication systems and services to it or to an occupier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(1): the developer or owner has contravened the prohibition` MEANS
    `the developer or owner enters into or enforces an agreement or arrangement with an occupier that restricts or prevents the occupier from selecting any supplier of telecommunication systems and services` OR `the developer or owner enters into or enforces an agreement or arrangement with a telecommunication licensee that restricts or prevents other licensees from installing their installation, plant or system in the land or building, or supplying telecommunication systems and services to it or to an occupier`

-- src:2251 | (2) The Authority may give such directions as the Authority thinks
-- src:2252 | fit to be observed by the telecommunication licensee, or the
-- src:2253 | developer, owner or occupier of the land or building, to ensure
-- src:2254 | compliance with subsection (1).
@ref s 26(2) (src:2251-2254)
GIVEN `the direction is to ensure compliance with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(2): the Authority may give the direction to the telecommunication licensee, or the developer, owner or occupier` MEANS
    `the direction is to ensure compliance with subsection (1)`

-- src:2258 | (3) To avoid doubt, the Authority may give directions under
-- src:2259 | subsection (2) even though such directions may prejudice the
-- src:2261 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:2262 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 46
-- src:2264 | contractual obligations of the telecommunication licensee, or the
-- src:2265 | developer, owner or occupier of any land or building, whether the
-- src:2266 | obligation relates to a contract made before, on or after 1 February
-- src:2267 | 2017.
@ref s 26(3) (src:2258-2267)
GIVEN `the direction under subsection (2) may prejudice contractual obligations, whether the contract was made before, on or after 1 February 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(3): the prejudice to contractual obligations bars the Authority from giving the direction` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:2271 | (4) No liability shall lie against any party to a contract made before,
-- src:2272 | on or after 1 February 2017 for or in relation to, any breach of the
-- src:2273 | contract where the breach is solely attributable to, or occasioned by,
-- src:2274 | the compliance by that party with any direction of the Authority under
-- src:2275 | subsection (2).
@ref s 26(4) (src:2271-2275)
GIVEN `the breach of the contract is solely attributable to, or occasioned by, the party's compliance with a direction of the Authority under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(4): the party is liable for the breach of the contract` MEANS
    NOT `the breach of the contract is solely attributable to, or occasioned by, the party's compliance with a direction of the Authority under subsection (2)`

-- src:2279 | (5) Subsection (4) does not affect the operation of the Frustrated
-- src:2280 | Contracts Act 1959.
@ref s 26(5) (src:2279-2280)
GIVEN `the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959 would otherwise operate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(5): subsection (4) affects the operation of the Frustrated Contracts Act 1959` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:2284 | (6) The Authority may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the
-- src:2285 | whole or any part of a direction given under subsection (2).
@ref s 26(6) (src:2284-2285)
GIVEN `the Authority varies, suspends or revokes the whole or any part of a direction given under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(6): the Authority may at any time vary, suspend or revoke the direction` MEANS
    `the Authority varies, suspends or revokes the whole or any part of a direction given under subsection (2)`

-- src:2289 | (7) Any person who fails to comply with any requirement in a
-- src:2290 | direction under this section shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 26(7) (src:2289-2290)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with a requirement in a direction under section 26` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26(7): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    `the person fails to comply with a requirement in a direction under section 26`

-- src:2298 | 27. If any dispute arises under sections 15(2), 16(2), 17(1), 20(2),
-- src:2299 | 22(3) and 24(4), it shall, on application for that purpose by any
-- src:2300 | aggrieved person to the Authority, be determined by the Authority.
@ref s 27 (src:2298-2300)
GIVEN `the dispute arises under section 15(2), 16(2), 17(1), 20(2), 22(3) or 24(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggrieved person applied to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 27: the dispute is to be determined by the Authority` MEANS
    `the dispute arises under section 15(2), 16(2), 17(1), 20(2), 22(3) or 24(4)` AND `the aggrieved person applied to the Authority`

-- src:2308 | 28. The execution of any work by a public telecommunication
-- src:2309 | licensee under this Act which may affect any street, railway, river,
-- src:2310 | canal, or other waterway or any system of irrigation, drainage or
-- src:2311 | water supply or any telecommunications, harbour works or any other
-- src:2312 | public or private works, and the erection of any installation or plant
-- src:2313 | used for telecommunications whether over, on or under the ground
-- src:2315 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:2316 | 47 Telecommunications Act 1999 2020 Ed.
-- src:2318 | must be carried out in a lawful manner having regard to the safety of
-- src:2319 | any person or property.
@ref s 28 (src:2308-2319)
GIVEN `the work is by a public telecommunication licensee under the Act and may affect a street, railway, river, canal or other waterway, a system of irrigation, drainage or water supply, telecommunications, harbour works or other public or private works, or is the erection of installation or plant used for telecommunications over, on or under the ground` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is carried out in a lawful manner having regard to the safety of any person or property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28: the public telecommunication licensee has carried out the work as the section requires` MEANS
    (NOT `the work is by a public telecommunication licensee under the Act and may affect a street, railway, river, canal or other waterway, a system of irrigation, drainage or water supply, telecommunications, harbour works or other public or private works, or is the erection of installation or plant used for telecommunications over, on or under the ground`) OR `the work is carried out in a lawful manner having regard to the safety of any person or property`

-- src:2325 | 29.—(1) The installation or plant used for telecommunications of a
-- src:2326 | public telecommunication licensee shall not be subject to distress or
-- src:2327 | be liable to be taken under or pursuant to an enforcement order under
-- src:2328 | any process of a court in any bankruptcy or insolvency proceedings
-- src:2329 | against any person without the Minister’s prior written approval.
@ref s 29(1) (src:2325-2329)
GIVEN `the installation or plant is the public telecommunication licensee's installation or plant used for telecommunications` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister gave prior written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29(1): the installation or plant is subject to distress, or liable to be taken under an enforcement order in bankruptcy or insolvency proceedings` MEANS
    `the installation or plant is the public telecommunication licensee's installation or plant used for telecommunications` AND `the Minister gave prior written approval`

-- src:2333 | (2) Every installation or plant used for telecommunications placed
-- src:2334 | under, over, along, across, in or upon any property by a public
-- src:2335 | telecommunication licensee remains the property of the licensee
-- src:2336 | concerned whether or not it has become in whole or in part a fixture.
@ref s 29(2) (src:2333-2336)
GIVEN `the installation or plant used for telecommunications was placed under, over, along, across, in or upon property by a public telecommunication licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29(2): the installation or plant remains the property of the licensee, whether or not it has become in whole or in part a fixture` MEANS
    `the installation or plant used for telecommunications was placed under, over, along, across, in or upon property by a public telecommunication licensee`
